(6594646, 983873, 124190, '<td valign="top">great shot....looks like the door just opened and it''s time to get the fire started....can really feel the expectation and hope of warming up soon....also the cold.....soon to be warm inside.   great in b&amp;w...good grain....top 3</td>', 'great shot....looks like the door just opened and it''s time to get the fire started....can really feel the expectation and hope of warming up soon....also the cold.....soon to be warm inside.   great in b&w...good grain....top 3', '2011-11-14 13:19:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6594655, 983140, 124190, '<td valign="top">Lovely colors and grain.  I am rather new to DPC.......so if I may ask a question....not to be taken as a criticism....rather a point of discussion.   This rule of thirds......sometimes it seems disconcerting to me.     Why would I so much liked to have seen more of the image to the left of the cat and less of the right side of the image?   I know the composition should work with the line of the cliff and waves but IMhumbleO it left the left side heavy.   Do you have another shot standing back behind the cat so that the head would be to the right of the jetty.....or one with a tad less crop to the left?  I would love to see the other shots in this photo shoot. Would you post them somewhere? Still beautiful....high mark.</td>', 'Lovely colors and grain.  I am rather new to DPC.......so if I may ask a question....not to be taken as a criticism....rather a point of discussion.   This rule of thirds......sometimes it seems disconcerting to me.     Why would I so much liked to have seen more of the image to the left of the cat and less of the right side of the image?   I know the composition should work with the line of the cliff and waves but IMhumbleO it left the left side heavy.   Do you have another shot standing back behind the cat so that the head would be to the right of the jetty.....or one with a tad less crop to the left?  I would love to see the other shots in this photo shoot. Would you post them somewhere? Still beautiful....high mark.', '2011-11-14 13:35:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6594656, 983754, 124190, '<td valign="top">wonderful!   I love the composition....the way you saw the bookbag juxtaposed against the walk way boards..... was the child coming home from or going to school?   either way there seems to be some reluctance...hesitation or maybe even exhaustation..... can "see" so much in the posture even from behind.....just lovely....sweet capture and great editing....my favorite. 10</td>', 'wonderful!   I love the composition....the way you saw the bookbag juxtaposed against the walk way boards..... was the child coming home from or going to school?   either way there seems to be some reluctance...hesitation or maybe even exhaustation..... can "see" so much in the posture even from behind.....just lovely....sweet capture and great editing....my favorite. 10', '2011-11-14 13:35:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6594657, 983787, 124190, '<td valign="top">my favorite shot....would have liked to see a little more grain....but still my fav.    9</td>', 'my favorite shot....would have liked to see a little more grain....but still my fav.    9', '2011-11-14 13:35:07.000000', NULL, 1),
