(6596620, 983655, 16241, '<td valign="top">nostalgic (for me anyway)</td>', 'nostalgic (for me anyway)', '2011-11-16 15:33:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596637, 983574, 30364, '<td valign="top">Beautifully constructed picture.  All the lines, smears and vapors make strange connections, as if we''re seeing things here that are normally not visible.  I''m moved to imagine a guardian angel in the form of a long-deceased grandmother, or something along those lines.  And the oblivious fellow on the right is perfect; he''s there, but this small scene is not for him. He doesn''t even know it''s happening.  An absorbing photograph.  Thank you.</td>', 'Beautifully constructed picture.  All the lines, smears and vapors make strange connections, as if we''re seeing things here that are normally not visible.  I''m moved to imagine a guardian angel in the form of a long-deceased grandmother, or something along those lines.  And the oblivious fellow on the right is perfect; he''s there, but this small scene is not for him. He doesn''t even know it''s happening.  An absorbing photograph.  Thank you.', '2011-11-16 15:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596638, 983140, 30364, '<td valign="top">Lovely, rebellious, anti-photography kind of photograph.  What a relief!  Thank you.</td>', 'Lovely, rebellious, anti-photography kind of photograph.  What a relief!  Thank you.', '2011-11-16 15:48:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596639, 983823, 30364, '<td valign="top">Good thought you had to use grain in a context where perfection of rendering is the norm.  And to such very good effect, too!  It''s lovely.  Thank you.</td>', 'Good thought you had to use grain in a context where perfection of rendering is the norm.  And to such very good effect, too!  It''s lovely.  Thank you.', '2011-11-16 15:48:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596640, 983787, 30364, '<td valign="top">Excellent picture where the grain plays a supporting rather than dominating role.  You''ve used a piccolo rather than a tuba, and so the effect is light, beautiful and melodious - rather than just a loud and dissonant fart.  Thank you.</td>', 'Excellent picture where the grain plays a supporting rather than dominating role.  You''ve used a piccolo rather than a tuba, and so the effect is light, beautiful and melodious - rather than just a loud and dissonant fart.  Thank you.', '2011-11-16 15:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596643, 982870, 30364, '<td valign="top">Epic human landscape.  So here''s a Thumb in your eye!  <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Epic human landscape.  So here''s a Thumb in your eye!  ', '2011-11-16 15:50:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596645, 983915, 30364, '<td valign="top">In my top three because it''s such a wonderfully interesting and restless picture.  There''s no way a viewer can just glance at this and be satisfied; it <i>demands</i> more engagement than that!  Does the grain enhance that effect?  Yes, of course.  So does the fact that it''s (unusually) in colour.  As does the part-concealed face.  As does everything, really.  It''s a superb, durable, marvelously <i>open</i> photograph!  You''ve made the photograph (rather than the thing being photographed) the champion.  That''s a lamentably rare thing at DPC.  Thank you.  And please accept an Order of the Thumb: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'In my top three because it''s such a wonderfully interesting and restless picture.  There''s no way a viewer can just glance at this and be satisfied; it demands more engagement than that!  Does the grain enhance that effect?  Yes, of course.  So does the fact that it''s (unusually) in colour.  As does the part-concealed face.  As does everything, really.  It''s a superb, durable, marvelously open photograph!  You''ve made the photograph (rather than the thing being photographed) the champion.  That''s a lamentably rare thing at DPC.  Thank you.  And please accept an Order of the Thumb: ', '2011-11-16 15:53:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596646, 983714, 30364, '<td valign="top">Wonderful faces, all the more eloquent for their nearly negligent representation here.  Very satisfying composition, all triangles, lines, connections and disconnections, but <i>never</i> formulaic (you''d hardly know the ''composition'' was there, it''s so unforced and natural).  Brilliant tonal palette.  And grain that a film photographer would adore.  All in all, there''s nothing better in the challenge.  10, and a big Thumbs Up from me<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a>.</td>', 'Wonderful faces, all the more eloquent for their nearly negligent representation here.  Very satisfying composition, all triangles, lines, connections and disconnections, but never formulaic (you''d hardly know the ''composition'' was there, it''s so unforced and natural).  Brilliant tonal palette.  And grain that a film photographer would adore.  All in all, there''s nothing better in the challenge.  10, and a big Thumbs Up from me.', '2011-11-16 15:53:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6596685, 983842, 11518, '<td valign="top">Beautiful subject but over-processed. Halo on the right side of the train and no grain is present.</td>', 'Beautiful subject but over-processed. Halo on the right side of the train and no grain is present.', '2011-11-16 17:21:57.000000', NULL, 1),
